  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "authentication",
      "title": "Two verification stages",
      "items": [
        "Challenge processing verifies the Apple attestation chain, freshness, required device identifiers, and configured admission policy.",
        "Finalization checks the CSR signature, reverifies stored evidence against the CSR public key, and rechecks device binding and admission policy before signing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "certificate",
      "title": "Certificate retrieval",
      "items": [
        "Signed requests consume one-use replay nonces. A finalized order provides a certificate URL that the client retrieves using POST-as-GET.",
        "Issuance commits a receipt before registration. Registration failure leaves a recoverable processing order; finalize retry or order polling rechecks key, expiry and admission and reuses the same certificate. Download is blocked until registration completes.",
        "SCEP and ACME identity issuance are independent of the HTTPS trust anchors distributed for enrollment endpoints."
      ]
    },
    {
